    "field": "Decadal climate prediction",
    "problem": "This paper addresses challenges in predicting Atlantic decadal climate variability, stemming from an incomplete understanding of its physical drivers, significant model biases, and poor representation of teleconnections that propagate predictive skill from the ocean to land areas.",
    "method": "This paper is a review article that surveys recent progress, foundations, and frontiers in understanding and predicting Atlantic decadal climate variability; it does not propose a new, specific method.",
    "task": "The task is to survey the foundations and frontiers in understanding Atlantic decadal variability mechanisms and the present capacity for putting that understanding into practice in actual climate prediction systems.",
